{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133321-merit-about-your-avatar-being-new-did-i-just-make-this-up","id":1133321,"title":"Merit about your Avatar being \"New\"; did I just make this up?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-24T04:51:33-07:00","id":1133321,"title":"Merit about your Avatar being \"New\"; did I just make this up?","content":"I distinctly remember reading a Mage Merit where your Avatar is 100% new and has never incarnated before. It made the character Extra Special and required that you buy at least one dot in True Faith, and I think it also required that the Mage be a child. Does anyone know where I read this? I believe it was an M20 book but I can't find it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T05:53:43-07:00","id":1133340,"title":"","content":"Huh. I don't remember a merit like that.<br /> But I also don't see why a brandnew avatar should require a child, plus True Faith on top.<br /> <br /> I'll rummage through the texts some to see if I can find what you are thinking of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T06:20:30-07:00","id":1133344,"title":"","content":"Nope, can't find anything related to True Faith, I'm afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T06:43:39-07:00","id":1133352,"title":"","content":"Having a new Avatar sounds like an interesting idea, but why on earth would it be connected to True Faith or childhood? It sounds like you might be mixing several different merits. I wouldn't be surprised if there was a merit that gave you true faith because you were a child. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, there might be a Flaw that makes you a child widderslainte incapable of true faith.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T07:02:28-07:00","id":1133358,"title":"","content":"Having a new Avatar, as an idea, might be better represented through interpretation and other Traits that a particular Merit. Your Avatar it's a rookie, he won't be able to teach (nor torment) you trough Past Lives, and your character won't have Merits or Defects related to past incarnations. On the other hand it's recent &quot;birth&quot; may be a sign of a potent Destiny. Socialy, the very idea that an Avatar can be born it's a mind blowing insight into the misterious nature of Avatars that may attract the atention of Spirit erudites, if this fact gets to be known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-24-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:46:14-07:00","id":1133425,"title":"","content":"I found it! It isn't a Merit. I combed through BoS because I was sure I had read it there, and when I moved past the Merits I found it later in the book.<br /> <br /> It's in the Book of Secrets section on Child Mages. There are a few types, and one type is the Innocents.<br /> <br /> Innocents are Mages with Brand New Avatars. They are rare and tend to have Destiny, connections to a High Umbral spirit etc. etc. They are pre-teens as a rule (I think the implication is that they are a recent development, something New) and they have True Faith between 1 and 3 to represent their strong beliefs and child-like innocence, but this can be in anything.<br /> <br /> My assumption is that they are linked to the World of Darkness trending towards oblivion in the modern setting, with Apocalypse/Gehenna/etc. on the horizon. This means we need saviours, and some higher forces (possibly something from the High Umbra) have conspired to produce prodigies who are innocent and pure, ready to shepherd mankind, but that's just my take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-24-2017, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:30:49-07:00","id":1133440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133321-merit-about-your-avatar-being-new-did-i-just-make-this-up?p=1133425#post1133425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My assumption is that they are linked to the World of Darkness trending towards oblivion in the modern setting, with Apocalypse/Gehenna/etc. on the horizon. This means we need saviours, and some higher forces (possibly something from the High Umbra) have conspired to produce prodigies who are innocent and pure, ready to shepherd mankind, but that's just my take.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say you need more than innocence and purity to avert cataclysmic events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}